    "final_text": "I fixed every problem in the incident report, all in `src/inventory.js`. The full suite passes with the fix (15 tests). With the fix stashed, the 7 new tests in `tests/concurrency.test.js` give 5 failures, so those tests do reproduce the problems.\n\n**Causes and fixes**\n- **Oversell, negative `reserved`, double holds on retry:** every method read a counter, waited on the store, then wrote it back, so concurrent workers overwrote each other's updates. All read-modify-write operations (`addStock`, `reserve`, `commit`, `release`, `expire`) now run one at a time through a lock. The lock is per store, so several service instances sharing a store also serialize. It only covers a single process, so workers running as separate processes would still race.\n- **Bundle item left held after a rejection:** `reserve` held each item as it went, so a later out-of-stock item left the earlier ones held. It now checks every item first and only holds them once all pass.\n- **`sold` too high and `reserved` negative:** `release` accepted committed orders and put their units back, and `expire()` released committed and already-released orders too. `release` now throws `OrderStateError` for a committed order, and `expire()` only releases orders that are still reserved.\n\nThe public API and error classes are unchanged, and `src/store.js` is untouched. I did not commit anything.",
